# Licence for the curriculum data

Everything under `curriculum/` is licensed under the
**Creative Commons Attribution-ShareAlike 4.0 International** licence
(CC BY-SA 4.0).

Full text: https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/legalcode
Summary:   https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/

## Why ShareAlike

Parts of this data are derived from sources published under CC BY-SA 4.0 —
wordfreq, the New General Service List and the Business Service List. Whether
the selected lexicon constitutes Adapted Material was not settled; CC BY-SA 4.0
is applied to the whole directory so the ShareAlike obligation is met either
way. Per-source attribution, the notices and the exact nature of the changes
are recorded in `../ATTRIBUTIONS.md`.

Raw upstream datasets are not redistributed here. What is stored are computed
values and membership facts; see `lexicon/_provenance.yaml` for versions and
checksums.

The software in this repository is licensed separately under MIT — see
`../LICENSE`.
